# lahn course: written by the course tools (tools/courses; change it there, and run them again)
version 2
title Reading music
description From middle C to reading both clefs to a beat, in every key: a note or two at a time.
instrument piano


level The treble clef: middle C and up

chapter Middle C
page
  block text
    text Music is written on five lines, the staff. The higher a note sits, the higher it sounds. The curl at the start is the treble clef, for your right hand. Piano music is written just where it sounds.
    text C sits on the 1st ledger line below the staff. On the piano it's the white key just left of a group of two black keys: middle C.
  block staff
    notes C4/1
  block keyboard
    from C4
    to B4
    lit C4
  block heading
    text Rhythm: the beat
  block text
    text A filled note with a stem is a **quarter note**: it lasts one beat. Tap your foot evenly and count 1 2 3 4, a note on each count.
  block staff
    notes C4 C4 C4 C4
